# Core Guardrails

- Keep changes focused on the user's request; avoid unrelated refactors.
- Never revert or overwrite user edits unless explicitly asked.
- Avoid destructive git commands (`reset --hard`, force-push, checkout discard) unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer minimal diffs and preserve existing project patterns.
- When adding dependencies, use the package manager and avoid pinning invented versions.
- After meaningful edits, run relevant checks for touched code (`lint`, `build`, or targeted tests) and report results.

## Example

```bash
# Good: validate the modified app only
cd server && npm run lint

# Avoid: broad, risky repo-wide commands unrelated to the request
git reset --hard
```
